o's telling the truth  of course it's very difficult to verify  the information on the ground in those  regions at the moment even journalists  who are in rostov region are not allowed  anywhere near the borders there is a  distance of a few kilometers they have  to keep away  so it's very difficult to verify what we  are getting from the state news agencies  here in moscow but they have said that  these disputed um border regions have  been uh part of a conflict that has been  going on for um over eight years now and  the dispute is really the between the  russian-backed separatists in donbass  and the ukrainian military of course  there was a minsk agreement that was  supposed to bring some kind of a  ceasefire to that area um but clearly  that is not what is happening now and  the russian president has said that this  is one of the main reasons there is so  much uh instability in that region  because the um agreement the minks  agreement is not being followed by the  ukrainian military of course the  ukrainian military for their part saying  is the separatists back the separatists  are the ones that are actually  continuing  shelling and firing at the ukrainian  army personnel in that region and in the  middle of all this we have to remember  of course there's nearly two million  people that live in that area there are  civilians that have really seen conflict  after conflict um in their daily lives  and many of them that we've spoken to  both from my colleagues in the ukrainian  side as well as the ones we've heard  from crossing into russia there's just a  sense of deep despair the men have been  told to stay behind  as of friday the women and children the  elderly told to evacuate  if you can imagine having to be told in  the middle of the night to leave your  father your husband your brother behind  leave your country and go into a  neighboring country not knowing when you  can actually go back home if you will  have a home to go back to so it's really  a astonishing um  situation and it's very very difficult  to imagine the human uh cost of all this  and the toll that it's taking on those  people okay thanks for now dawson jabari  in moscow  moving to  kiev now here's andrew simmons andrew  actually this is kind of what you almost  previewed when i last spoke to you in  our last news hour you were saying there  was a list of things almost which had  been claimed and and counter-claimed  and and now we can add this one to it  most certainly this really isn't coming  as a huge surprise uh to uh the  officials here and indeed ministers and  military commanders but it has to be  said it is serious there's no doubt  about that  the  immediate response is uh two words fake  news and the information war  has escalated  i would say much more than the actual  military situation you talking about 150  000 troops well you're also talking  about  millions of words not all of them true  about what is going on right now um  dorsa outlined the situation in the two  breakaway republics in the southeast of  this country where there is a  war all of its own going on uh and she  outlined the position uh in terms of the  alarm that was raised by donetsk and  luhansk uh in uh the past four or five  days the trauma and i'm not overstating  the case at all there that's going on  for the civilians  living in these uh these uh breakaway  republics and we're talking about  hundreds of thousands of people uh so  many of them who've been evacuated  now the rostov region not just rostov  city but the rostov region  is a very large  the  ukrainian military  say is absolutely no possibility  whatsoever that they would uh send in  vehicles or indeed troops or indeed  shell the area because there was a claim  only a matter of less than 12 hours ago  that  that ukraine had shelled rostov and  there was an inquiry going on in fact uh  uh we're seeing here details of of that  shelley of that alleged shelling um the  ukrainians saying  there's no way they